title: Friends of the Republic
subtitle: Build support for democracy beyond the Senate chamber.
is-card: true
tags: caucus_affairs
card-image: img/card_civil.svg
view-if: civil_timer <= 0 and date >= 24
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; civil_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "civil"
new-page: true

= Friends of the Republic

The Senate is not the Republic. Its strength lies with the billions who still believe in it: civic leagues, free journalists, teachers, veterans of the Judicial Forces.

- @networks: Build civic networks across member worlds.
- @holonet: Fund an independent HoloNet foundation.
- @clones: Campaign for the rights of clone troopers.
- @easy_discard

@networks
subtitle: −1 political capital. More faith; broader support for the Caucus.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.faith += 1.5; for (var i = 0; i < SW.REGIONS.length; i++) Q[SW.REGIONS[i] + '_rc'] += 0.7 * SW.unity(Q); !}

"Friends of the Republic" societies spring up on hundreds of worlds.

@holonet
subtitle: −1 political capital. Protects the free press; harder to silence later.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; free_press += 1; faith += 0.5; evidence += 0.2

An independent HoloNet foundation, funded from a dozen worlds, begins broadcasting from Chandrila.

@clones
view-if: clones > 0
subtitle: The clones trust the Senate more; the Security Bloc objects.
on-arrival: clone_trust += 1; navy_loyalty += 3; sec_relation -= 3; faith += 0.5

The Caucus asks a simple question in the Senate: are the clone troopers citizens of the Republic they die for? Nobody has a good answer.
